Actually, there are 4 types of gems in vanilla Nethack which match that 
description before being identified:  Luckstones, loadstones, 
touchstones, and flint stones.  Only touchstones identify other gems 
(and themselves).  Also, the ID property only works if it's blessed, or 
if you are a gnome or an Archaeologist and it's at least uncursed.

Loadstones are really heavy, and autocurse when picked up, requiring 
remove curse to drop.  If they are on the ground, and you kick them 
without kicking boots, they don't move, and you hear 'Thump'.
Luckstones and touchstones are worth more to shopkeepers.
Flint stones, although making good sling ammo, are worthless to shopkeepers.

So, kick test any gray stones you see, if they move, pick em up.  If a 
shopkeeper (general, jeweler, or tool) offers to buy them, bless them. 
Then rub against an unidentified gem.  If it doesn't ID, you just 
blessed a luckstone, keep it in your inventory for good luck.  If it 
does, then it's a touchstone, and the game will tell you so.

If the shopkeeper from the previous step doesn't want it, or is selling 
it for 1 (or 2?), then it's a flint stone.

